Added an address preference to GitHub providers: an ordered list of `@domain` entries and `*` that decides which of an account's addresses becomes the `email` claim and the order a new profile lists them in. Linking by email now tries every address a provider verified, in that order, instead of the first one only; when two of them belong to different accounts, the higher-ranked one wins and the conflict is logged. A site can also ask a person whose first sign-in brought more than one verified address which of them stands for them: with the new `confirm_email_at_first_login` setting on, their profile stays incomplete until they answer through the new `POST @confirm-email` endpoint, and `@my-profile` reports the question as `confirm_email`. @ericof
